sidebar:
  label: "KoboldAI Lite"
  order: 1
---

KoboldAI Lite is the web interface built into KoboldCpp. After you click **Launch**, it opens at `http://localhost:5001`. You need nothing else to chat, write stories or play text adventures.

<!-- SCREENSHOT: KoboldAI Lite right after launch, top menu visible -->

## Start chatting

{% steps %}

1. Launch KoboldCpp with a model. With **Launch Browser** ticked (the default in the launcher), Lite opens by itself. Otherwise, open `http://localhost:5001`.
2. Type into the input box at the bottom and send.
3. To change how Lite behaves, click **Settings** in the top menu.

{% /steps %}

## Modes

Pick the mode in **Settings** > **General** > **Usage mode**.

| Mode | Use it for |
|---|---|
| **Instruct Mode** | Giving the AI tasks, ChatGPT-style. |
| **Chat Mode** | Conversations with a character. |
| **Story Mode** | Novel-style writing, where you and the AI write the same text. |
| **Adventure Mode** | Interactive fiction and text RPGs. |

## UI styles

Next to the mode, **UI style** changes how the text is shown. Some styles are only available in some modes.

| Style | Look |
|---|---|
| **Classic Theme** | Plain text editor, for writing. |
| **Messenger Theme** | Chat bubbles. |
| **Aesthetic Theme** | Roleplay layout. The button next to it opens more display options. |
| **Corpo Theme** | Assistant-style layout. |

## Where the settings are

The launcher decides what the server can do: which model, how much context memory is reserved, which features are loaded. Lite decides what it sends with each request.

**Settings** has these tabs:

| Tab | What you find there |
|---|---|
| **General** | Usage mode, UI style, your name and the AI's name. |
| **GUI** | Appearance. |
| **Samplers** | **Sampler Preset**, **Context Size**, **Max Output**, **Temperature** and the other samplers. |
| **Media** | Image generation, text-to-speech (**Audio Output**) and voice input (**Audio Input**). |
| **Tokens** | Token settings. |
| **Tools** | MCP tool calling and web search. |
| **Misc** | Save/load, advanced and experimental settings. |

**Context Size** in Lite covers the text Lite sends plus the reply (**Max Output**). The server cuts it down to the context it reserved at launch. If the server reserved 16384 or more, Lite raises its own value to match. A value you lowered yourself stays until the server's context changes. See [Context size](/docs/settings/context-size/).

The other top menu items:

- **New Session** starts over.
- **Scenarios** loads ready-made stories and characters.
- **Save / Load** saves and loads your story as a JSON file.
- **Context** (above the input box) holds memory, world info and the author's note.
- **Add File** (above the input box) adds images or audio, or generates an image.

## Other bundled interfaces

| Address | Interface | Available when |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | KoboldAI Lite | Always. |
| `/sdui` | StableUI, for images | Always. Generating images needs an image model. See [Image generation](/docs/features/image-generation/). |
| `/musicui` | MusicUI, for music and speech | Always. Generating needs a music or TTS model. See [Music](/docs/features/music/). |
| `/lcpp/` | The llama.cpp web UI | Always. It can connect to MCP servers. |
| `/noscript` | A plain page without JavaScript, with story, chat and image modes | Always. For old or restricted browsers. |
| `/api` | The API documentation | Always. |

If you load only an image model, Lite offers to open StableUI. If you load only a music or TTS model, it offers MusicUI.

## Lite without KoboldCpp

Lite also runs at [lite.koboldai.net](https://lite.koboldai.net). That copy can connect to your KoboldCpp, to the AI Horde, or to online AI services.

To use the bundled Lite without a local model, tick **Allow Launch Without Models** on the **Loaded Files** tab (`--nomodel`). Lite then asks whether to connect to an external service.

## Advanced

- **TextDB** (**Context** > **TextDB**) is Lite's document lookup (RAG). **Local TextDB** searches in the browser. **KoboldCpp Embeddings** uses the loaded [embeddings model](/docs/features/embeddings/).
- Lite loads Tavern character cards, and imports SillyTavern chat exports (JSONL) and several other save formats.
- In **Settings** > **Samplers**, **Sampler Preset** switches between curated sampler sets.

